<title>JAPAN: Nippon Paper to up stake in Weyerhaeuser venture.</title>
<headline>Nippon Paper to up stake in Weyerhaeuser venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Paper Industries Co Ltd said on Wednesday it had agreed with Weyerhaeuser Co to raise its stake in their newsprint joint venture North Pacific Paper Corp (NORPAC).</p>
<p>The Japanese firm said in a statement that it will raise its stake in the joint venture to 50 percent from the current 20 percent by the end of March 1998. But specific terms of the purchase will be decided by the end of 1997, it said.</p>
<p>Through the purchase, Nippon Paper will be able to actively expand its business overseas, it said.</p>
</text>
